The block's scenarios are all implemented and tested:
- schema header and strictness;
- location and id patterns;
- 1–20 hops;
- closed enums;
- the three required model rejections (paths.py:181-186, :163-168);
- `write_paths_file`'s four steps;
- the argument checks before any call (paths.py:378-384);
- `./` normalisation;
- null cap when unscoped;
- fallback recorded as skipped;
- exports and the dependency plus lock;
- the D1 rows 6/7/9/10 spec amendments.

Gaps:
- The pydantic models still parse in lax mode, so `PathsResult.model_validate` accepts documents the schema rejects (e.g. `scoped: "false"`, `line: "3"`). This is safe on the write path but looser than the contract on the read path.
- The amended 'Test-listing shape' text says each array is sorted by `(file, line, node_id)` and each `node_id` appears at most once in it, but neither the model nor the schema enforces this. It is left to later producers.
